{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build","id":808356,"title":"What SHOULD Abyssals Be Able To Build?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T18:16:14-08:00","id":808356,"title":"What SHOULD Abyssals Be Able To Build?","content":"I was about to ask this question improperly; I was going to ask what Abyssals are able to build, but given their current state in 2e (specifically the fact that ceratin charms were limited to &quot;destructive&quot; artifacts), I might not get a satisfactory answer. So here goes: What should Abyssals be able to build? Should they be as good at building as Solars, just in different ways? Or are they truly limited in this respect because of their connection to death and entropy? If you had 300 like-minded Abyssals, would you have something like the First Age, just painted black? Or is such a thing impossible, or just more difficult without Solars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:28:15-08:00","id":808359,"title":"","content":"Abyssals should excel at building mausoleums, crypts, tombs, pyramids (that are really just big tombs), and of course gibbets. [/facetious]<br /> <br /> Really though - I figure that Abyssals should be able to build anything a Solar would. The manner in which they might do so differs, but that doesn't mean they can't be constructive, either literally or metaphorically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:41:07-08:00","id":808367,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure what they'd end up building would be a Creation of eternal war where all the cultures are warrior ones, emphasizing valor, courage and dying in battle so that they'd end up in the afterlife made by the Abyssal they serve, filled with tombs, mausoleums to pray in, to fuel the afterlife paradises they hope to someday join, mandatory sacrifices, bloody gladiatorial combat, skull decorations, just an endless cycle of life and death carefully calculated to make sure the Abyssals stay in power through the ghosts loyalty, assuming they try to sustain and perpetuate this for as long as they can. Peace would be unwelcome because it means they have to wait longer to get into the afterlife. Medicine men would be seen as jailers keeping them from seeing the rest of their family, and of course anyone with self-preservation would be seen as cowards and would probably think of themselves as cowards...things like that.<br /> <br /> It'd basically become Warhammer 40,000 without the technology. no I don't mean normal Warhammer, that is a different universe by now with its own tone. I mean WH40k, the universe of unendng war and people being so used to it they can't imagine anything else without the space opera tech. So yeah. not First Age at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:15:27-08:00","id":808413,"title":"","content":"Abyssals make whatever Solars make, except that their Essence seeps into their works, such that they are cursed (to the deathknights' benefit), or maddeningly beautiful, or corrupting in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T22:52:10-08:00","id":808473,"title":"","content":"Hold on there is a Monty Python Sketch about this that highlights two Abyssal Architects.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RicaXxiU1WM\" data-code=\"RicaXxiU1WM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RicaXxiU1WM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:56:56-08:00","id":808494,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Craft Charms should be limited to black make-up and My Chemical Romance tee shirts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:49:50-08:00","id":808502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808473#post808473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold on there is a Monty Python Sketch about this that highlights two Abyssal Architects.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RicaXxiU1WM\" data-code=\"RicaXxiU1WM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RicaXxiU1WM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That first architect late died and received a black exaltation, unleashing a wave of abattoirs upon Creation!<br /> <br /> On a more serious not, Abyssals craft what ever they like, but most likely go for the whole thematic principle of darkness, decay, death, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:08:04-08:00","id":808526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808502#post808502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That first architect late died and received a black exaltation, unleashing a wave of abattoirs upon Creation!<br /> <br /> On a more serious not, Abyssals craft what ever they like, but most likely go for the whole thematic principle of darkness, decay, death, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that and the second one created a death trap that would kill about as many people as the first, while meaning to create something that wouldn't kill and bring death. So when I think Abyssal Craft I can't help but to picture there essence creeping in and turning anything they make into something that is just as likely to kill people or cause them to stagnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:38:04-08:00","id":808541,"title":"","content":"I think Abyssals will be capable of building almost anything, but their Charms will provide various rewards or discounts into the Craft system based on things like provoking Intimacies related to the chivalry of death, as well as maybe some things that are specifically made for killing or destroying. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had 300 like-minded Abyssals, would you have something like the First Age, just painted black?</div> </div> </div> </div> I say you would have the Age of Sorrows very efficiently transitioned into a graveyard. That's not a matter of their limitations so much as their inclinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:52:39-08:00","id":808544,"title":"","content":"As opposed to personally building, necessarily (although no doubt they have something in those directions), what I probably would be interested in is Abyssals who can:<br /> <br /> - protect other Exalted builders through destruction of problems in their way (the Wyld, ghosts, or more mundane problems)<br /> - as lords of entropy*, they can control the flow of entropy, away from what they wish to preserve in the world (but there is a balance, and Resonance); preservation is staying the hand of death away (unless that's much more Endings); they can be all like &quot;I pardon you&quot;.<br /> - dredge up ancient secrets, lost knowledge and ideas from the Underworld which assist others to build new things (even if in the sense of &quot;Do not do make the mistakes poor Pan-Khashi, Prince and Architect of Shammer did.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Fits OK with the role of certain Abyssals (like Soulsteels) as outriders like D.<br /> <br /> Although, for the collaboration aspects, I don't know how much the Craft systems in Exalted use this information? How well do collaborative building and construction projects with different players taking multiple roles in constructing the same object / artefact / etc actually work? A lot of what I hear and how I read the systems seems to suggest that Craft projects are always the product of this sole guy and not teams working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:22:49-08:00","id":808591,"title":"","content":"Honestly when it comes to Abyssals I think their crafting choices (like a lot of their choices really) are very limited.<br /> Not because of their themes, but because what they do is dictated by their Deathlord, or perhaps more accurately; their senior Abyssal.<br /> Right like it doesn't matter that your character could probably craft an amazing house to live in, their skills are needed elsewhere to bring death to Creation or whatever. Now what they're making may change; First and Forsaken Lion probably needs a lot of craftsmen making armor and weapons for their legion, while Bishop's exalts probably work on expanding his religion by building corrupt churches that brainwash whomever enters (meaning lots of intricate work with stone and wood carvings).<br /> <br /> I imagine that rebel Abyssals, or those who never got abducted by their Deathlord's minions in the first place, have a lot more freedom in what they craft and how their Abyssal-ness comes into effect.<br /> Probably have a lot of neat or odd little tricks to what they make that surprises the more loyalist dudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8495-peachyjams","name":"PeachyJams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8495_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:39:19-08:00","id":808597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what they do is dictated by their Deathlord, or perhaps more accurately; their senior Abyssal</div> </div> </div> </div> Hopefully not. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and Forsaken Lion probably needs a lot of craftsmen making armor and weapons for their legion</div> </div> </div> </div> So it's probably not a very good use of the ten or so Abyssals he'll have the allegiance of, of which <i>maybe</i> one is likely to be inclined towards crafting. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bishop's exalts probably work on expanding his religion by building corrupt churches that brainwash whomever enters</div> </div> </div> </div> It's all very reductive, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:28:46-08:00","id":808621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808591#post808591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly when it comes to Abyssals I think their crafting choices (like a lot of their choices really) are very limited.<br /> Not because of their themes, but because what they do is dictated by their Deathlord, or perhaps more accurately; their senior Abyssal.<br /> Right like it doesn't matter that your character could probably craft an amazing house to live in, their skills are needed elsewhere to bring death to Creation or whatever. Now what they're making may change; First and Forsaken Lion probably needs a lot of craftsmen making armor and weapons for their legion, while Bishop's exalts probably work on expanding his religion by building corrupt churches that brainwash whomever enters (meaning lots of intricate work with stone and wood carvings).<br /> <br /> I imagine that rebel Abyssals, or those who never got abducted by their Deathlord's minions in the first place, have a lot more freedom in what they craft and how their Abyssal-ness comes into effect.<br /> Probably have a lot of neat or odd little tricks to what they make that surprises the more loyalist dudes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for reminding me why Abyssals desperately need a rewrite.<br /> <br /> Not that I consider your summation particularly accurate for their 2e writeup, but just the fact that people do arrive at such conclusions warrants purging the current material with fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:29:41-08:00","id":808623,"title":"","content":"I'd expect that Abyssal craft will be a bit like the Solar tree, but with an emphasis on deconstruction and demolition with a bit of a boost for constructing new things from the wreckage they unleash, or for preserving/repairing something at the cost of the destruction of something else. I could also see Charms for things like getting more speed/productivity out of a team of assistants at the cost of their health and/or sanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:32:12-08:00","id":808624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808621#post808621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for reminding me why Abyssals desperately need a rewrite.<br /> <br /> Not that I consider your summation particularly accurate for their 2e writeup, but just the fact that people do arrive at such conclusions warrants purging the current material with fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. These kinds of limitations are better for NPC-only characters, not PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:07:42-08:00","id":808800,"title":"","content":"Isn't that what abyssals are though?<br /> Like... they're just skilled minions of whatever Deathlord exalted them.<br /> As they were explained to me when you play an Abyssal you either play a Loyalist who's okay with serving their Deathlord and ushering in the end of Creation, someone who serves a particular Ancestor Cult, a rebel who's either smart enough to realize that the Deathlords are powerful questionably sane ghost tyrants and lucky enough to escape/want to be Solars. Or you are playing a murder-hobo kept alive by the Neverborn as an instrument against the Deathlords should they turn traitor... or something like that.<br /> I may be simplifying down what I was told, but is this not what people make Abyssals for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8495-peachyjams","name":"PeachyJams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8495_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:59:04-08:00","id":808851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808367#post808367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no I don't mean normal Warhammer, that is a different universe by now with its own tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:17:15-08:00","id":808875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808800#post808800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what abyssals are though?<br /> Like... they're just skilled minions of whatever Deathlord exalted them.<br /> As they were explained to me when you play an Abyssal you either play a Loyalist who's okay with serving their Deathlord and ushering in the end of Creation, someone who serves a particular Ancestor Cult, a rebel who's either smart enough to realize that the Deathlords are powerful questionably sane ghost tyrants and lucky enough to escape/want to be Solars. Or you are playing a murder-hobo kept alive by the Neverborn as an instrument against the Deathlords should they turn traitor... or something like that.<br /> I may be simplifying down what I was told, but is this not what people make Abyssals for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, yes, and it's all a very thin basis on which to hang a PC splat. These are not issues if all Abyssals are NPCs and I am unconvinced that isn't where they should be at this point.they just have not been done well. I have the same opinion with some of the OWOD fera. It's ok for some things to not be PC options!<br /> <br /> I'd rather a splat be written well as thematic NPCs than be sloppy slapdash PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-14-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:25:20-08:00","id":808884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808800#post808800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what abyssals are though?<br /> Like... they're just skilled minions of whatever Deathlord exalted them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not quite, at least in the upcoming edition. From what the devs have said, the focus will be on loyalists as slaves or lackeys, but as the Deathlords' <i>knights</i>, their <i>prot\u00e9g\u00e9es</i>, their right hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:40:15-08:00","id":808893,"title":"","content":"The abyssal fluff line about only making weapons or destructive items is not actually mechanically binding, it just throws a road block in place for people who are not especially creative.<br /> <br /> Consider the following three scenarios:<br /> <br /> <b>1: </b>An abyssal could forge a sword (a weapon designed specifically for killing), and then only use it as a kitchen knife for preparing sumptuous meals out of extra large animals and vegetables. In this case a weapon is never used for destructive purposes, in fact it is used to enhance life. From this you can take away the concept that what it is used for after the fact doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <b>2:</b> An abyssal could crafter a truly fine quill or other writing implement, not inherently a weapon, but it gives a bonus for written social checks. The abyssal uses it to gain treaties that destabilize the enemies of the abyssals deathlord, thus causing wars and boarder squirmishes that wipe out hundred if not thousands of lives. As such it makes the pen many times more lethal than a sword wielded by an individual warrior.<br /> <br /> <b>3:</b> An Abyssal creates a necklace of incredible beauty and gives it to the youngest of three royal daughters of a random country. This leads to jealousy between the daughters and eventually family members start killing each other to possess the item. The item has no weapon value on its own, but given the human drive to possess things, such an item can be quite deadly.<br /> <br /> In the last two scenarios an otherwise innocuous item can be used to great effect, thus turning them into truly potent weapons.<br /> <br /> For my two cents, the abyssal crafting fluff line should be used as a narrative guide. The ST should ask the player what and how the item will be destructive or glorify death, if they have a decent answer then you go with it. If the Player is just wanting something cool they saw in an anime, movie or other media that really has nothing to do with death then I would suggest that they use it for a different character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:17:26-08:00","id":808931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808623#post808623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect that Abyssal craft will be a bit like the Solar tree, but with an emphasis on deconstruction and demolition with a bit of a boost for constructing new things from the wreckage they unleash, or for preserving/repairing something at the cost of the destruction of something else. I could also see Charms for things like getting more speed/productivity out of a team of assistants at the cost of their health and/or sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesomely flavorful.<br /> <br /> For my part, I just apply a fog machine and black spray paint to Solars' capabilities and call it a night.<br /> <br /> More seriously though, I tend to make my Abyssals just a shade less powerful than my Solars, so they have to go further out of their way to create staggeringly powerful artifacts and the absolute most ridiculous stuff (that would require Herculean efforts from Craft-dedicated Solars) I keep out of their reach, but that is 100% my personal taste in how I prefer my setting. But, otherwise, they're imbued with S<i>olar frickin' exaltation</i>, and that lends itself to plenty of immensely effective wonder-making. Heck, in my current game a Daybreak antagonist is scavenging the shadowlands of Chiaroscuro for materials and reagents with which to to build a necromantic engine that imbues the dead with terrible sorcerous power. Given that my PC's have switched focus to playing Burgeoning Desert Kingdom Sim, this artifact is likely going to be unleashed without a hitch, and it has a decent chance of giving that Abyssal enough raw power to make a serious play for Chiaroscuro itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:33:41-08:00","id":809099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeesun</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">imbues the dead with terrible sorcerous power</div> </div> </div> </div> What form does that power take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:46:55-08:00","id":809208,"title":"","content":"Well, they are playing up the &quot;Deathknight&quot; thing this time, so I doubt Abyssals will be walking entropy sprinklers again. I'm sure they will still have Necrosurgery and Necromancy in their wheelhouse. But, I think a fair number of the hyper-limiting restrictions will fall away. Abyssals exist to advance the power of the Underworld/dead, not necessarily to just annihilate Creation.<br /> <br /> If you mentally erase the Neverborn from your understanding of Exalted, it's much easier to see the Deathlords and their mad passions and their ploys for power, and how the Deathknights work within that. There are hundreds of potentially great stories that don't involve &quot;Destroy every living thing I see all the time murderdeathkillmurderdeathkill.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember, the big players are being pushed into the background so everyone gets narrative freedom. That includes Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:06:15-08:00","id":809225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809208#post809208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they are playing up the &quot;Deathknight&quot; thing this time, so I doubt Abyssals will be walking entropy sprinklers again. I'm sure they will still have Necrosurgery and Necromancy in their wheelhouse. But, I think a fair number of the hyper-limiting restrictions will fall away. Abyssals exist to advance the power of the Underworld/dead, not necessarily to just annihilate Creation.<br /> <br /> If you mentally erase the Neverborn from your understanding of Exalted, it's much easier to see the Deathlords and their mad passions and their ploys for power, and how the Deathknights work within that. There are hundreds of potentially great stories that don't involve &quot;Destroy every living thing I see all the time murderdeathkillmurderdeathkill.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember, the big players are being pushed into the background so everyone gets narrative freedom. That includes Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, they wouldn't be entropy sprinklers.<br /> <br /> just to clarify my own view: a Creation ruled by a bunch of necromancers whose power involve zombies and ghosts, probably isn't one we'd think of as safe, full of long prosperous lives or peaceful. It doesn't matter if the world under Abyssal rulership succumbs to a slow long entropy or continues on forever stable, it would still involve the Abyssals trying to take full advantage of their powers to to re-order society around them, problem is, those are powers of death. which means the societies would be re-ordered around death. which leads to death. and thus probably end up being an eternal engine of war and sacrifice to power ghostly paradises. But hey look on the bright side! No one outside Creation is attacking you anymore! I mean who would be crazy enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:18:41-08:00","id":809236,"title":"","content":"Necrosurgery is going to have to look very different, because necrotech (aka &quot;magitech with corpses&quot;) is going to have to be pared into the themes of &quot;magitech and the visuals associated with it: pretty much not a Thing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:32:23-08:00","id":809301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809099#post809099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What form does that power take?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad someone asked!<br /> <br /> The powers of each Recreated (my antagonist's brand name for them) are contingent on the character and strength of the Ties and Intimacies of the person used to create them. Sadists produce revenants with especially dangerous weapons of made of essence and bone, or which gain physical bonuses at the sight of blood. A couple deeply in love might enjoy powerful bonuses to each others' combat abilities when in proximity. A grieving parent or despised vagrant might have a gaze or poison that induces mind-wracking loneliness and ennui. Someone that believed that all people are truly good inside might be able to induce powerful feelings of trust and compassion in their enemies. Which Intimacy each Recreated is formed from is at the discretion of whoever is attuned to the artifact at the time, and the process itself costs time and essence to initiate and complete. The revenants obey the will of their creator so long as this creator remain attuned to the engine that created them, (not that he knows that little detail yet) and are possessed of about as much cunning and ferocity as a Xenomorph.<br /> <br /> This is what has been driving this antagonists' partner, a stealthy, brutal Dusk caste, to venture out into the city under disguise and find the most passionate and committed of its citizenry to murder. The Dusk seeks out those in the throes of great passions or sorrows: sadists, virtuosos, lovers, masters, new parents of slain children (more often than not, slain by the Abyssal's hand), and saints. Then, once the Daybreak's engine is complete, they will create an army of powerful Recreated revenants and strike quickly and brutally at the heart of Chiaroscuro. Based on the profane lore my antagonist has gathered, the combination of the necromantic workings he has been performing at set intervals throughout the Chiaroscuro shadowlands and enough slaughter and fear in a single night will cause the boundaries of the Shadowlands to expand and begin to consume the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T21:02:04-08:00","id":809352,"title":"","content":"There's a problem with the premise of the question. The Crafting rules are very much designed so that the Exalted don't need Charms to make things; there's no Solar Charm to make legendary First Age manses or artifacts. The closest you get is Dual Magnus Prana, and that's a capstone Charm. <br /> <br /> I would expect to see Charms that give Abyssals dice tricks and additional project slots and crafting points if they're working in the Underworld or in Shadowlands, and it seems likely that the Abyssal Repair tree will focus on breaking things or reforging them so that they can be attuned to the Essence of the Underworld - like rebuilding a temple so that it honours the Deathlords instead of its intended god, or breaking an orichalcum daiklave so that it can be used as a component for a soulsteel daiklave - but I don't have any better ideas. Maybe some Charms to protect grave goods so they're not dissolved by sunlight, like a reverse Chaos-Resistance Preparation? Assuming sunlight melting grave goods actually a thing - I don't really remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T07:16:13-08:00","id":809562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PeachyJams</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=808800#post808800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what abyssals are though?<br /> Like... they're just skilled minions of whatever Deathlord exalted them.<br /> As they were explained to me when you play an Abyssal you either play a Loyalist who's okay with serving their Deathlord and ushering in the end of Creation, someone who serves a particular Ancestor Cult, a rebel who's either smart enough to realize that the Deathlords are powerful questionably sane ghost tyrants and lucky enough to escape/want to be Solars. Or you are playing a murder-hobo kept alive by the Neverborn as an instrument against the Deathlords should they turn traitor... or something like that.<br /> I may be simplifying down what I was told, but is this not what people make Abyssals for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say even with the subpar fluff we've been given on them, this is a horribly reductive view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:45:54-08:00","id":809615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809352#post809352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a problem with the premise of the question. The Crafting rules are very much designed so that the Exalted don't need Charms to make things; there's no Solar Charm to make legendary First Age manses or artifacts. The closest you get is Dual Magnus Prana, and that's a capstone Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way of expressing an issue I've been having.<br /> <br /> I think this makes me interested to see what the Craft Charms for Dragon Blooded will be like, since that might be a good indicator of where it stands. I do think it's possible that they might get a mix of less powerful modifiers for the Craft system, some straightforward &quot;make local elemental thing&quot; Charms, and maybe some of their old sapper powers, but I'll wait and see.<br /> <br /> Might also be good to see what new Exalted might do with it, since as it is the Dragon Blooded are the only ones really operating in the same wheelhouse as the Solars and their fellows (since Lunars don't have Abilities and Sidereals don't really use Craft to make things, although perhaps that's another thing that may be altered slightly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">breaking things or reforging them so that they can be attuned to the Essence of the Underworld - like rebuilding a temple so that it honours the Deathlords instead of its intended god, or breaking an orichalcum daiklave so that it can be used as a component for a soulsteel daiklave</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> These feel like more things in that area of not needing Charms to do, to me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Another thing that's a bit uncertain for the moment is the status of those Craft Charms to interact with Evocations, since they're obviously going to be revised massively. It may be that their new form could give ideas for something distinct to Abyssals and Dragon Blooded (possibly more for the latter, since they might have more facility with Evocations in general).<br /> <br /> Still, even without that, we do have a certain precedent for Craft as an Ability to draw new power out of something. Combine that with necromantic stuff in general and Deathlord capstones in particular, and there may be something to giving motion to some large horror. Maybe even more directly integrate some of that elaborate corpse machines thing that was a bit shaky before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:13:06-08:00","id":809634,"title":"","content":"First off, I think Abyssals shouldbe able to make anything they want. The only Exalted who I feel may be somewhat limited in that respect might be certain unique Exigents who, depending on their patron might find it difficult to craft certain things or channel Essence to assist with working with certain substances.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, I would like their Crafting to heavily incorporate themes like memories, things forgotten, horror and Ideas That Should Not Exist. Anything crafted by an Abyssal should be perfectly serviceable, but also have something wrong, disturbing or creepy about it (either subtly or overtly).<br /> <br /> A portrait by an Abyssal would be just as impressive as one made by a Solar, but perhaps the eyes really do follow you, or sometimes if you stare at it for too long, an odd series of handprints seem to appear on it but vanish when you stop to look.<br /> <br /> These sorts of effects would help to instill certain Intimacies in people and are a natural result of the inherent <i>wrongness </i> of the Abyssal bleeding out into his creations.<br /> <br /> In general I think Abyssals should be great at creating things that instill madness, death, fear and despair, or that carry curses, perhaps getting bonus crafting exp or other breaks when making something like that, buy they definitely shouldn't take penalties (or face limitations) for crafting something useful, helpful or that doesn't focus on those themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T09:59:36-08:00","id":809668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809615#post809615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These feel like more things in that area of not needing Charms to do, to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of? I'm thinking more about something like a Charm that gives Abyssals, I don't know, 50 automatic successes to a craft project when they use pieces of a broken 4-dot Artifact to make a 5-dot Artifact, essentially allowing Abyssals to &quot;steal&quot; successes or maybe crafting points from items they break. If Abyssals want to craft better and bigger stuff, they also need to destroy better and bigger stuff to get their momentum going. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure that fits the portrayal of Ex3 Abyssals though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:33:27-08:00","id":809741,"title":"","content":"Here's my wishlist for Abyssal Crafting:<ul><li>That ghost story thing where a ruined house looks whole and welcoming for the night or tattered robes that are beautiful while the ghost wears them</li> <li>The curse on Harmonia's necklace that caused the events of, like, three epics, or as Charles Stross put it: &quot;the nature of the curse was that it would cause blood to be spilled&quot;</li> <li>Tempering a sword in blood/sharpening it by running it through a sacrifice, etc</li> <li>skull architecture</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T12:35:36-08:00","id":809789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809634#post809634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In general I think Abyssals should be great at creating things that instill madness, death, fear and despair, or that carry curses, perhaps getting bonus crafting exp or other breaks when making something like that, buy they definitely shouldn't take penalties (or face limitations) for crafting something useful, helpful or that doesn't focus on those themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, <i>that</i> is interesting in terms of the possibility of modifying how Craft interacts with Intimacies. Indeed, for the idea of Abyssals making murderous or destructive things... imagine if, instead of being better at it, you had an Abyssal who would get Crafting XP when their products are used in such a manner, even long after the Abyssal has made it? Kind of putting yourself into the applications of your work.<br /> <br /> Even other things it could do... if instead of &quot;I build a church to the Deathlords&quot; (which anybody could do), it's that you build a church and then reap certain benefits from it being used in rites to the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> I'm getting an image of a certain spectral link between an Abyssal and the things that she makes; it reminds me of those preview Presence Charms, and it's a lot more moving to me then the idea that it improves making deadly things alone did.<br /> <br /> Here was me just extending the idea of Mirrors to Evocation bringing Charms being more than zombie machines in the manner of, say, anointing some Gothic statuary that you made yourself with your blood, which then seeps into the masonry and spreads out lines of tendon and sinew and bone in order to give the thing motion as a servant and guardian. Maybe the power of such depends on how much blood you give it, with something comparable to a Solar's divine familiar if you Incapacitate yourself in the process (the Abyssal won't actually die, but they'll be torpid and vulnerable for a while).<br /> <br /> Maybe even give our stone beast a perfunctory bronze helmet, which is ineffectual and purely decorative on account of the fact that its skin is made of stone, it doesn't need a helm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking more about something like a Charm that gives Abyssals, I don't know, 50 automatic successes to a craft project when they use pieces of a broken 4-dot Artifact to make a 5-dot Artifact, essentially allowing Abyssals to &quot;steal&quot; successes or maybe crafting points from items they break. If Abyssals want to craft better and bigger stuff, they also need to destroy better and bigger stuff to get their momentum going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now, if it's a case of &quot;doing these particular things interacts with the system differently&quot; rather than just &quot;they can do these things&quot;, that's a horse of a different colour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:00:29-08:00","id":809807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809789#post809789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, <i>that</i> is interesting in terms of the possibility of modifying how Craft interacts with Intimacies. Indeed, for the idea of Abyssals making murderous or destructive things... imagine if, instead of being better at it, you had an Abyssal who would get Crafting XP when their products are used in such a manner, even long after the Abyssal has made it? Kind of putting yourself into the applications of your work.<br /> <br /> Even other things it could do... if instead of &amp;quot;I build a church to the Deathlords&amp;quot; (which anybody could do), it's that you build a church and then reap certain benefits from it being used in rites to the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> I'm getting an image of a certain spectral link between an Abyssal and the things that she makes; it reminds me of those preview Presence Charms, and it's a lot more moving to me then the idea that it improves making deadly things alone did.<br /> <br /> Here was me just extending the idea of Mirrors to Evocation bringing Charms being more than zombie machines in the manner of, say, anointing some Gothic statuary that you made yourself with your blood, which then seeps into the masonry and spreads out lines of tendon and sinew and bone in order to give the thing motion as a servant and guardian. Maybe the power of such depends on how much blood you give it, with something comparable to a Solar's divine familiar if you Incapacitate yourself in the process (the Abyssal won't actually die, but they'll be torpid and vulnerable for a while).<br /> <br /> Maybe even give our stone beast a perfunctory bronze helmet, which is ineffectual and purely decorative on account of the fact that its skin is made of stone, it doesn't need a helm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well now, if it's a case of &amp;quot;doing these particular things interacts with the system differently&amp;quot; rather than just &amp;quot;they can do these things&amp;quot;, that's a horse of a different colour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh I really like the direction you and Anubis have suggested here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:07:38-08:00","id":809890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=809789#post809789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, <i>that</i> is interesting in terms of the possibility of modifying how Craft interacts with Intimacies. Indeed, for the idea of Abyssals making murderous or destructive things... imagine if, instead of being better at it, you had an Abyssal who would get Crafting XP when their products are used in such a manner, even long after the Abyssal has made it? Kind of putting yourself into the applications of your work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm liking where this idea is going.<br /> <br /> I've always been a fan of the idea that Abyssals are dark mirrors to Solars, though typically this was often more of a mechanical, &quot;Just like Solars but evil,&quot; than anything else. Still, the idea of Abyssals approaching certain ideas from a different direction than Solars does appeal to me.<br /> <br /> For a Solar craftsman, the bulk of his inspiration (Craft exp) comes from the actual act of crafting. He makes something and gets XP to make something else. In general the idea of what the object is used for didn't seem to play a big factor. While a Solar crafter might make something with a goal in mind, it is ultimately the act of creation that causes his soul to tremble.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that this is in inverted among the Abyssal. Just spitballing, but for them, the use of the object takes priority. So an Abyssal might make a sword, or a suit of armor, or a waterwheel, but the act of crafting doesn't inspire her. Rather, the inspiration would happen when the object actually gets used. So while, for a Solar, crafting is itself the goal, for an Abyssal it's merely a means to an end. This creates a philosophical and mechanical inversion of the way a Solar approaches crafting without making it an &quot;evil opposite.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps Abyssals could even gain bonuses when objects are used towards specific ends, like defending the Underworld or serving their lieges goals. Perhaps there might even be a Charm that allows Abyssal to create an object for a specific task, giving them extra bonuses if it does: this daiklave has been forged to slay the Behemoth Choclis, the Ever Present, granting a bonus to the Abyssal's craft XP if that happens (though that might be better for a Sidereal craftsman whose weapons and creations might carry specific fates).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:29:26-08:00","id":809990,"title":"","content":"I think any Abyssal Craft tree is going to have a variety of directions it goes in. There's no reason to just have one &quot;abyssal craft&quot;; we want a charmset, not one charm.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> <br /> Crafting stuff by wrecking your environment and consuming natural resources (think Saruman in LotR -- a sort of vague metaphor for industrialization, though without the industrialization.) Cutting down an entire forest or strip-mining an entire mountain to craft a single artifact. Boiling away an entire lake to get a few drops of elemental water that you need for your artifact. &quot;Price of progress&quot;-style charms.<br /> <br /> Drawing forth ancient things that have been destroyed or lost from beyond the veil of death -- maybe altered somehow by their passage. The Crown of Thunders was lost forever in the First Age, but you can recreate it as the Crown of Echoing Silence or the like. Maybe also bonuses to creating artifacts intended to memorialize or remember the dead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:33:10-08:00","id":810241,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how this would work mechanically, but maybe a charm that could invest a created item with a vague malevolence, allowing weapons to be used better and allowing non-weapon items to be more easily employed as weapons, like a necklace that seems to almost squirm to the touch, and seems to almost squeeze the victim's throat when used as a garrote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T00:39:15-08:00","id":810523,"title":"","content":"While PeachyJams isn't 100% right about the reductive quality of Abyssals in 2e, they also aren't <i>wrong</i> and that should really be a concern for us moving into 3e. I often found myself playing Abyssal Daybreaks who used nasty or lethal <i>components</i> when crafting just because it met that &quot;destructive&quot; requirement that goes into everything abyssals make using their craft time reduction charm. I felt that if I played true to the theme of the charm then all I would be able to play was &quot;weaponsmith&quot; and if I wanted to explore concepts beyond that then the game had simply written in an extra road block for me to overcome, and not in a fun way.<br /> <br /> Looking ahead I'm hoping we see more of the Deathknights as &quot;Underworld Exalts&quot; and less murder machines, though murder machine will I'm sure remain a valid option and should remain so. Perhaps charms that allow you to destroy something in Creation but create a perfect, timeless replica of it in the Underworld? Charms that break down items into useful components also feels thematic. Ironically I could see charms both for crafts that take longer but last forever AND for crafts that produce wondrous artifacts in a fraction of the time but which wilt into nothingness in a few days.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Solars should remain the craftiest of crafters and the most sorcerous of sorcerers, and so I won't be disappointed if Abyssals can't do everything their Solar counterparts can. Whereas a Solar gets charms that provide permanent Superior projects slots, I don't see the Abyssals becoming steady engines of forward progress. Perhaps they can take an existing artifact and destroy it to make a single-use superior project slot? And whereas &quot;innovation&quot; is a hallmark of Solar crafting I imagine that Abyssal essence balks at the creation of truly new things, but when working from a known blueprint they can steadily reforge wonders lost to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T05:36:38-08:00","id":810586,"title":"","content":"So here's what I've got: Abyssals should be able to build ANYTHING they want with a few caveats: While they can build anything at all, they will only be able to build <b>certain things</b> as <b>quickly</b> as Solars, their essence bleeds into their work (giving it a horrifically beautiful, or maddening quality) which could have inimical effects on those who use the item or those around it, they're better at reclaiming lost wonders rather than creating new ones (not to say they couldn't), and they can really get their craft going after deconstructing something for spare parts. Hm... That sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Personally, I think Solars should remain the craftiest of crafters and <b>the most sorcerous of sorcerers</b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Yeah (though I'm not sure where Infernals are supposed to fit in there). and Abyssals would be the most necromatic of necromancers.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:56:52-08:00","id":810828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=810586#post810586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah (though I'm not sure where Infernals are supposed to fit in there). and Abyssals would be the most necromatic of necromancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I had honestly forgotten about Infernals, but I would think that they could compete with Solars in certain areas thematic to their Yozi with spellcraft, but not in all areas. In general though I'm hoping we see more from this design space of excelling in different areas than we do the tired &quot;solars are good at everything so how are we downgrading the other solaroids?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:49:46-08:00","id":811076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=810586#post810586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's what I've got: Abyssals should be able to build ANYTHING they want with a few caveats: While they can build anything at all, they will only be able to build <b>certain things</b> as <b>quickly</b> as Solars, their essence bleeds into their work (giving it a horrifically beautiful, or maddening quality) which could have inimical effects on those who use the item or those around it, they're better at reclaiming lost wonders rather than creating new ones (not to say they couldn't), and they can really get their craft going after deconstructing something for spare parts. Hm... That sounds pretty cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah (though I'm not sure where Infernals are supposed to fit in there). and Abyssals would be the most necromatic of necromancers.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know how productive it'll be to speculate on Infernals at this stage, given how little information we even have about the Yozi in this edition, but I rather liked the 2E take on them where a new Infernal has to get their head around the alien logic of the Yozi whose power they're channeling in order to get the most of their abilities. I'm going to assume that the 'charms are not an IC thing' take on this edition is going to necessitate some major changes in that regard though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T06:32:30-08:00","id":811085,"title":"","content":"I think the application of most Yozi Charms was fairly straightforward. The Excellency, maybe that was one that demanded much lateral thinking. Something like the Malfeas cascade... you had a bunch of Charms for enhancing attacks and soak, and a couple that directly changed how your brain worked; it demanded little of the Infernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T06:49:38-08:00","id":811089,"title":"","content":"Eh, when I played an Infernal I found they did work a bit like that. Not in terms of how the charms worked (except for the excellencies) but in getting the best use out of them. They were a bit like Sidereal charms, where you had to come at things in slightly indirect ways. Less so, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T08:20:17-08:00","id":811134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LDjuPZJpG4A\" data-code=\"LDjuPZJpG4A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LDjuPZJpG4A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> It's very 2e but I've long held this up as my go-to example of Abyssal Craft because it goes back to Obadiah Stane's memetastic rant from the first film about how a team of scientists couldn't do what Tony Stark did, despite having access to a working version of the same technology. Ivan Vanko basically does his own evil version of the cave with a box of scraps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-18-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:34:14-08:00","id":811202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811085#post811085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the application of most Yozi Charms was fairly straightforward. The Excellency, maybe that was one that demanded much lateral thinking. Something like the Malfeas cascade... you had a bunch of Charms for enhancing attacks and soak, and a couple that directly changed how your brain worked; it demanded little of the Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; I didn't see a hell of a lot of <i>thinking </i>on the parts of Infernals in my GSP game, or instances of them saying &quot;How can I make this Charm apply?&quot; so much as bellowing &quot;DO AS I TELL YOU, SLAVES!&quot;, followed by crowns of green hellfire wreathing their heads. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:55:28-08:00","id":811217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811085#post811085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the application of most Yozi Charms was fairly straightforward. The Excellency, maybe that was one that demanded much lateral thinking. Something like the Malfeas cascade... you had a bunch of Charms for enhancing attacks and soak, and a couple that directly changed how your brain worked; it demanded little of the Infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant it more in the sense of 'how the heck do I apply my ability to do Weird Thing X to assist me in my actual goals, given my lack of interest in turning people into my mutant bug slaves or punching All The Things until they obey me?' The charms themselves aren't all that difficult to understand, but finding non-obvious ways to use them is a fun part of the process IMO. Some (many, it sounds like) would just make a character who DOES want to punchify all who defy them, which substantially simplifies things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:34:05-08:00","id":811327,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when a Zenith wants to convert a village to his cause, he can do it with one rousing speech if he has a couple Performance Charms.<br /> <br /> When a Malefactor wants to do the same, he'll probably have to spend a couple days there, granting people wishes and then forcing them to do what he needs as a repayment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:29:43-08:00","id":811367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechanlith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant it more in the sense of 'how the heck do I apply my ability to do Weird Thing X to assist me in my actual goals, given my lack of interest in turning people into my mutant bug slaves or punching All The Things until they obey me?'</div> </div> </div> </div> To me, that sounds more like a bug than a feature. I mean, if one was able to harness it to serve one's gameplay needs despite some design problems, more power to you. Just... it's how I would look on speculation for the future. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">when a Zenith wants to convert a village to his cause, he can do it with one rousing speech if he has a couple Performance Charms</div> </div> </div> </div> You're talking about Second Edition, right? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Malefactor wants to do the same, he'll probably have to spend a couple days there, granting people wishes and then forcing them to do what he needs as a repayment.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's interesting, given the social system we have now, and the ways that Solars interact with and are limited by it, I think there could be some ways to make Infernals converting or commanding people distinct in concept and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T02:09:11-08:00","id":811619,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'm talking about 2e - not much point in comparing 2e Infernals with 3e Solars, is it?<br /> <br /> In general, I'd say 2e Solars had a lot of Charms that were like &quot;if you want to do X, here's a Charm that directly helps you do X&quot;. With Infernals, it was more like &quot;here's a Charm that does something, now you have to figure out how to use it to do X&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:33:11-08:00","id":811707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811619#post811619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I'd say 2e Solars had a lot of Charms that were like &quot;if you want to do X, here's a Charm that directly helps you do X&quot;. With Infernals, it was more like &quot;here's a Charm that does something, now you have to figure out how to use it to do X&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>(double-checks Crowned With Fury)<br /> <br /> Um...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:38:20-08:00","id":811713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811707#post811707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(double-checks Crowned With Fury)<br /> <br /> Um...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because bringing up particular Charms that work against the trend negates the existence of the trend entirely, right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:40:46-08:00","id":811742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811713#post811713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because bringing up particular Charms that work against the trend negates the existence of the trend entirely, right.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally one of the first social Charms in the Infernals book, but sure, let's go over some of the others.<br /> <br /> Impervious Primacy Mantle - straightforward and free mental defense, you can even spend motes to apply bonus MDV against social efforts outside its wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> Demonic Primacy of Essence - order around demons of lower Essence, or with extra Charms, gods of lower Essence. The most complicated thing you need to do here is avoid gods and demons of higher Essence.<br /> <br /> Sublimation of Ordained Purpose - tell gods and demons to do the jobs they were created to do. Not seeing any &quot;ponder seriously to make it apply.&quot;<br /> <br /> Knowing the Desolate Heart - auto-succeed at reading a target. Once again, in what situation is using this not straightforward?<br /> <br /> Unshattered Tongue Perfection, second purchase - use relative Essence instead of Appearance. If you're going Cecelyne, this is a great side-grab.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Transcendence of (Virtue) - adds one of four permanent mental perfects, among other things. As Isator said, less about making you think about how to use it and more about changing your thinking altogether.<br /> <br /> Joy in Violence Approach - gain bennies aborting out of social combat for Join Battle. Considering 2e social combat, this is, again, not particularly hard to justify using.<br /> <br /> Tragic Love Amusement - subject's MDV drops by your Compassion against your social attacks. Not merely applicable, but disgustingly so.<br /> <br /> Witness to Darkness - if you're the kind of PC who <i>takes</i> Witness to Darkness, it will never impede you, ever.<br /> <br /> Selfishness Is Power - if you're the kind of PC who takes Selfishness Is Power...<br /> <br /> Selfishness Is Power (x2) - okay, I admit, if you're the kind of PC who takes Selfishness Is Power twice, you might have to think about how to use it, maybe.<br /> <br /> Selfishness Is Power (x3) - if you've thought about how to use Selfishness Is Power's second purchase, no additional thought is necessary for how to use it when you've bought it a third time...<br /> <br /> Nemesis Self Imagined Anew - instantly know the target's Motivation by acquiring its opposite - if you don't want to keep it afterward, drop it, no thought required.<br /> <br /> Soul Crack Exploitation - just first make sure and enjoy your reduced target numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-19-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:13:21-08:00","id":811773,"title":"","content":"Are you going to list every Infernal Charm which does something fairly straightforward?<br /> <br /> Do you expect me to make a counter-list of Charms that do something you have to figure out yourself how to use in a given situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:45:54-08:00","id":811795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Witness to Darkness - if you're the kind of PC who takes Witness to Darkness, it will never impede you, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could also use a Background dot to get a Deceiver Stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:18:48-08:00","id":811816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/808356-what-should-abyssals-be-able-to-build?p=811773#post811773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going to list every Infernal Charm which does something fairly straightforward?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I <i>did</i> list most of the ones in which the word &quot;social&quot; appeared, even outside the Social Keyword. It's pretty clear that a GSP doesn't have to work particularly harder or take particularly longer or do particularly more thinking to achieve any but the most arbitrary social goal in 2e, and in many respects will find it easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:44:31-08:00","id":811836,"title":"","content":"And then you have the whole wish-granting tree, Chirality Prohibition Index, Our Little Secret... just off the top of my head. Charms that are ridiculously powerful, but which you'll never just whip out as a perfect, instant solution to your problem (unless your problem is &quot;I wish a bizarre cargo cult sprung up right here&quot; or something like that).<br /> <br /> Not that I wanted to limit the discussion to social stuff in the first place (Zenith vs Malefactor was the first example that came to my head, and it's kinda obvious combat Charms have to be relatively straightforward, as they have a rather rigid combat subsystem to work in), but I honestly don't think anything you've listed even begins to compare to the raw power and broad applicability of such Charms as Husband-Seducing Demon Dance or Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}